      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(synology-chat): bound outbound NAS response bodies to prevent Gateway OOM",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOutbound Synology Chat responses previously buffered response bodies without a byte cap, risking Gateway OOM within the request timeout. Inbound webhooks were already bounded.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **Chatbot POST (status-only):** success follows HTTP status; unused body is destroyed/discarded without buffering so a large 200 body cannot flip a successful send into a false failure or unbounded memory growth.\n- **user_list:** keep bounded body reads (1 MiB) with cache fallback on overflow.\n\n## Evidence\n\n**Current head:** `b70e6c0c`\n\n**Unit tests:**\n```\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts\n→ 24 passed\n```\n\n**Rank-up (P1):** large-body HTTP 200 chatbot responses succeed; response stream is destroyed without buffering.\n\n**Lint:** oxfmt + oxlint on touched files — clean\n\n## Review\n\n- ClawSweeper Rank-up: preserve status-only 200 success without buffering\n- AI-assisted: Yes\n",
